# Code owners for Goobers.
# Owners are requested for review automatically and, once branch protection (#3)
# requires CODEOWNER review, must approve before merge.
# Order matters: the last matching pattern wins.
#
# NOTE: as the project grows, replace @masra91 with an org team
# (e.g. @Agent-Clubhouse/maintainers) so ownership isn't tied to one account.

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
*                       @masra91

# Build/CI tooling — the enforced merge gate.
/.github/               @masra91
/Makefile               @masra91
/.golangci.yml          @masra91

# Tutor config-only write-boundary (#104 / T4). The dogfood instance's Tutor is
# path-scoped to two action roots (TUT-A5/#1217): reference-workflows/gaggles/goobers
# and skills/. Because Tutor PRs land in the same repo as platform code here,
# CODEOWNER review on those trees is the required human gate before a self-tuning
# config change merges (structural credential enforcement rides #35).
# skills/ has no rule of its own and is covered by the default `*` owner above;
# give it an explicit rule before narrowing or reassigning that default.
# See docs/guides/tutor-write-boundary.md.
/reference-workflows/    @masra91
